  "query_preview": "..\nThe leading edge of a trough extending northward from Invest 97W \n(west of Chuuk) is within proximity of the eastern coastal waters of\nthe Marianas. Gentle to moderate winds have gradually shifted from \nthe north to the northeast throughout today, which will become \neasterly on Sunday as the trough moves through the region the next \ncouple of days. Increased shower coverage and isolated thunderstorms \nare expected overnight and will peak on Sunday with locally heavy \nshowers possible accompanied with gusty winds. Then, southerly to \nsouthwesterly flow may follow, possibly maintaining speeds of 10 to \n15 mph with scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms at least \nuntil next weekend.",
